---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { LINKEDIN, RESUME_FILE } from '../site';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const resume = RESUME_FILE ? `${base}/${RESUME_FILE}` : '';
---
<Base title="About" description="Nick Little, marketing leader in connected-vehicle and public-safety technology.">
  <div class="about">
  <p class="kicker">{'// about'}</p>
  <h1>Hi, I'm Nick.</h1>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>I'm a marketing leader in connected-vehicle and public-safety technology. I've spent 11 years at B2B companies selling hardware-software products to technical buyers, fleet operators and government agencies: owning brand, building demand engines and tying marketing to pipeline.</p>
    <p>Over the last year I started building my own AI systems: agents that find the right customers in a CRM, audit and rebuild an ad account, and turn scattered data into reporting leadership can trust. I'm not an engineer. I build with Claude, and I write up what worked, what broke and what it cost.</p>
    <p>Before that I was a technology writer, published in Forbes and the HubSpot Sales Blog, which is probably why I still care how things read.</p>
    <p>You can reach me on <a href={LINKEDIN} target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn</a>.{resume && <> <a href={resume} download>Download my résumé (PDF)</a>.</>}</p>
  </div>
  </div>
</Base>
